Third-party licences of libhs_vision
====================================

libhs_vision-<rid>.so, the hs_vision library of hass-sharp-vision, statically links the Rust crates named below
and embeds two models. cargo-about made this list from Cargo.lock for the library's four Linux targets. Each licence
text is given once, followed by the crates and versions it covers; texts that differ only in their copyright lines
stay apart, because those lines go with the binary. The list also names the procedural macros and the crates they
use (such as serde_derive, syn and unicode-ident), which run while the library is built and are not linked into it;
`cargo tree -e normal,no-proc-macro` in native/ lists only what is linked. The models' licences come last.

